<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Accessibility Statement</h1>
<p class="mb-6">This accessibility statement applies to <a class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline" href="https://berryhouse.ca">berryhouse.ca</a>, the website of 🍓 Berry House.</p>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Commitment to Accessibility</h2>
<p class="mb-6">We are committed to ensuring digital accessibility for all users, including people with disabilities. We believe the web should be accessible to everyone, regardless of ability, and we continually work to improve the user experience for all visitors.</p>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Accessibility Features</h2>
<p class="mb-2">This website has been designed and developed with accessibility in mind, incorporating the following features:</p>

<h3 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-1">Structural Accessibility</h3>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-4">
  <li><strong>Semantic HTML:</strong> Proper use of HTML5 elements (<code>&lt;header&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;main&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code>) to provide clear document structure</li>
  <li><strong>Skip Links:</strong> A "Skip to main content" link at the top of each page allows keyboard users to bypass navigation</li>
  <li><strong>Headings:</strong> Logical heading hierarchy (h1–h6) to support screen reader navigation</li>
  <li><strong>Landmarks:</strong> ARIA landmarks and roles to identify major page regions</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-1">Visual Accessibility</h3>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-4">
  <li><strong>Colour Contrast:</strong> Text meets or exceeds WCAG 2.1 AA contrast ratios (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text), with dark/light theme parity</li>
  <li><strong>A11y Menu:</strong> Use the accessibility menu in the header to adjust font size, contrast, and motion preferences; preferences are saved in your browser</li>
  <li><strong>Responsive Design:</strong> Content adapts to different screen sizes and zoom levels</li>
  <li><strong>Focus Indicators:</strong> Clear visible focus states for all interactive elements</li>
  <li><strong>Reduced Motion:</strong> Reduced-motion mode and respectful animations</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-1">Keyboard Navigation</h3>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-4">
  <li><strong>Full Keyboard Access:</strong> All functionality is available via keyboard</li>
  <li><strong>Tab Order:</strong> Logical tab order that follows the visual layout</li>
  <li><strong>No Keyboard Traps:</strong> Users can navigate in and out of all components</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-1">Content Accessibility</h3>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-6">
  <li><strong>Alt Text:</strong> Meaningful alternative text for all informative images; decorative images marked appropriately</li>
  <li><strong>Link Text:</strong> Descriptive link text that makes sense out of context</li>
  <li><strong>Form Labels:</strong> All form inputs have properly associated labels</li>
  <li><strong>Plain Language:</strong> Plain-language content with clear hierarchy</li>
  <li><strong>Performance:</strong> Performance budgets to keep pages fast on low-end devices</li>
  <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> Privacy-respecting analytics; no invasive tracking</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Technical Standards</h2>
<p class="mb-2">This website aims to conform to:</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-4">
  <li><strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong> (Web Content Accessibility Guidelines)</li>
  <li><strong>Section 508</strong> (US federal accessibility standards)</li>
  <li><strong>EN 301 549</strong> (European accessibility requirements)</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-1">Technologies Used</h3>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-6">
  <li>HTML5 semantic markup</li>
  <li>ARIA (Accessible Rich Internet Applications) where appropriate</li>
  <li>CSS3 with accessibility considerations</li>
  <li>Minimal JavaScript with keyboard and screen reader support</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Known Limitations</h2>
<p class="mb-2">While we strive for full accessibility, there may be some limitations:</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-6">
  <li>Some older blog posts may not meet current accessibility standards</li>
  <li>Third-party content (embedded videos, social media widgets) may have varying accessibility levels</li>
  <li>We are continually working to identify and fix accessibility issues</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Feedback and Assistance</h2>
<p class="mb-2">We welcome feedback on the accessibility of this website. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement, please contact us:</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-4">
  <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></li>
  <li><strong>Contact Form:</strong> <a class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline" href="/contact/">/contact</a></li>
</ul>

<h3 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-1">Reporting Issues</h3>
<p class="mb-2">When reporting accessibility issues, please include:</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-4">
  <li>The URL of the page where you encountered the issue</li>
  <li>The nature of the accessibility barrier</li>
  <li>The assistive technology or browser you were using</li>
  <li>Any steps to reproduce the issue</li>
</ul>
<p class="mb-6">We will make every effort to respond to accessibility feedback within 5 business days and address issues in a timely manner.</p>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Ongoing Efforts</h2>
<p class="mb-2">Accessibility is an ongoing commitment. We regularly:</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-6">
  <li>Test the site with screen readers and keyboard-only navigation</li>
  <li>Review new content for accessibility before publishing</li>
  <li>Stay updated on accessibility best practices and guidelines</li>
  <li>Audit the site periodically with automated and manual checks to identify and fix issues</li>
</ul>

